  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bambulab/BambuStudio/tarball/v02.08.02.61",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bambulab/BambuStudio/zipball/v02.08.02.61",
  "body": "Bambu Studio 2.8.2.61 is a minor optimization update based on the previous version. It fixes several known issues and improves the experience of certain features.\r\n\r\nYou can download the Flathub version for Linux from [Bambu Studio on Flathub](https://flathub.org/en/apps/com.bambulab.BambuStudio)\r\nThe Flathub version is maintained by @hadess , thanks to him for his outstanding work.\r\n\r\n## Bug Fixes\r\n1.  Fixed an issue where some MakerLab generators were inaccessible. (Note: Relief Maker downloads may experience import delays; a fix will be deployed via a subsequent MakerLab backend update.)\r\n2. Fixed an issue where the login window did not appear when accessing MakerWorld while not signed in.\r\n3. Fixed an issue where, after clicking “Sync Printer Information” in older 3MF files, the number of extruders could still be displayed as 0, which could further lead to slicing errors.\r\n4. When adding or removing filaments from the filament list on the left side of the Prepare page, the list will now automatically scroll to the bottom. This helps prevent users from mistakenly thinking the operation did not take effect when the filament list is long.\r\n5. Fixed an occasional crash in LAN mode under unstable network conditions.\r\n6. Updated presets for X2D and H-series printers, fixing several abnormal parameter values to prevent issues when loading or using the presets.",
